<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">Opening Current Account Without GST</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p><strong>GST is NOT mandatory</strong> for opening a current account. Banks require entity/business verification, and GST is one proof - but not the only one.</p><p><strong>Alternative proofs accepted:</strong> CA turnover certificate (with UDIN), Udyam/MSME registration, Shop & Establishment license, ITR acknowledgement, professional registration (Bar Council, Medical Council, ICAI).</p><p><strong>GST thresholds:</strong> Goods: Rs 40 lakh aggregate turnover. Services: Rs 20 lakh. Businesses below threshold are not required to register for GST.</p><p><strong>Best package:</strong> CA turnover certificate + Udyam registration = strongest combination for banks. Patron provides both.</p><p><strong>When to get GST:</strong> Once you cross the threshold or need GST for B2B invoicing. Patron handles GST registration when ready. See <a href="/gst-registration">GST Registration</a>.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for Turnover Certificate for Current Account in Gurugram:</strong></p>
                    <p><strong>Current Account:</strong> Business bank account for commercial transactions. No interest. Unlimited transactions. Minimum balance required.</p><p><strong>Entity Proof:</strong> Document proving your business exists and operates. GST, Udyam, Shop Act, or CA certificate.</p><p><strong>Udyam Registration:</strong> Free MSME registration from government. Serves as entity proof + MSME benefits. Patron assists.</p><p><strong>ITR-Based Certificate:</strong> Turnover from filed Income Tax Return. Strongest basis. Recommended.</p><p><strong>Bank Statement-Based:</strong> Turnover estimated from business deposits in bank statement. Weaker but acceptable when ITR not filed.</p>

